\newlabel{fig:2015-radfrac}{{14}{22}{Dedicated 2015 radiative-fraction inputs. The left panel shows the selected cross-section composition, while the right panel shows the radiative fraction used for normalization. The red horizontal line denotes the 8.5\% constant adopted as the conservative fit across the 2015 prompt-search dataset. This quantity converts the measured prompt spectrum into the expected $A^\prime $ normalization, so it affects the final $\eps ^2$ interpretation rather than the local spectral fit itself.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
