\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {24}{\ignorespaces Illustrative toy-limit diagnostic at fixed mass. The left panel shows a background-only ensemble of observed CL$_\mathrm  {s}${} upper limits, and the right panel shows the corresponding empirical cumulative distribution. The vertical line marks the observed limit. The lower-tail area defines $p_{\mathrm  {strong}}$, the upper-tail area defines $p_{\mathrm  {weak}}$, and $p_{\mathrm  {two}}=\qopname  \relax m{min}[1,2\qopname  \relax m{min}(p_{\mathrm  {strong}},p_{\mathrm  {weak}})]$ is used only as a symmetric diagnostic summary.\relax }}{40}{figure.caption.28}\protected@file@percent }
