\newlabel{fig:v5-individual-tails}{{45}{75}{Empirical limit-tail diagnostics for each dataset. Unrefined points use 300 toys; selected coordinates use the saved independent 3,000- or 10,000-toy batches. Open downward triangles show one-sided 95\% Monte Carlo upper bounds when no tail event is observed; for the two-sided diagnostic the bound is doubled and capped at one. These probabilities refer to the upper-limit statistic and are distinct from local asymptotic $p_0$.\relax }{figure.caption.57}{}}
